# StreamChat Overlay — Architecture & Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  subgraph Config ["Command Deck UI (index.html)"]
    A[Configure Platform Usernames & IDs] --> B[Pick from 10 Pro Gamer HUD Themes]
    B --> C[Customize Typography, Opacity, Stroke & FM Audio Profiles]
    C --> D[Test Live with Interactive Stream Test Deck & Soundboard]
    D --> E[Select OBS Resolution Preset & Copy Secure URL]
  end

  subgraph Engine ["Runtime HUD Engine (overlay.html)"]
    F[Read URL Search Parameters] --> G[Initialize 10 HUD Themes & Custom CSS]
    G --> H[Connect Multi-Platform WebSockets / REST API]
    H --> I[60+ Emote Dictionary + 7TV / BTTV / FFZ Live Engine]
    I --> J[BigEmote Scaler & Word Censorship Filter]
    J --> K[Hardware-Accelerated 60fps Animations & Queue]
    K --> L[Multi-Tier Event Alerts & Procedural FM Synthesizer]
  end

  subgraph Stream ["OBS Studio / Streamlabs"]
    M[Add Browser Source with URL] --> N[Overlay Appears with Transparent Background]
    N --> O[Crisp High-Contrast HUD Floating Live on Stream]
  end

  E --> F
  L --> M
```

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Streamer as Streamer (Browser / OBS)
  participant Deck as Command Deck (index.html)
  participant Overlay as Overlay HUD (overlay.html)
  participant Platforms as Twitch / YouTube / Kick APIs
  participant EmoteAPIs as 7TV / BTTV / FFZ CDNs

  Streamer->>Deck: Select Theme & Parameters
  Deck->>Overlay: postMessage({ kind: 'config_update' })
  Overlay-->>Deck: Reactive Live Preview Updated (Zero Lag)
  
  Streamer->>Deck: Click '💬 Chat' or '🎁 Gift' in Test Deck
  Deck->>Overlay: postMessage({ kind: 'chat' / 'event' })
  Overlay->>Overlay: Play Procedural FM Synth Tone & Animate Card

  Streamer->>Overlay: Launches Browser Source in OBS Studio
  Overlay->>Platforms: Connect Twitch (IRC) + YouTube (API) + Kick (Pusher)
  Overlay->>EmoteAPIs: Fetch 7TV, BTTV, FFZ Channel & Global Emotes
  Platforms-->>Overlay: Incoming Chat Messages & Hype Events
  Overlay->>Overlay: Parse Badges, Emotes, BigEmotes & Render 60fps HUD
```

